The logic to check whether Netflix is installed has been updated. The implementation now uses tizen.application.getAppInfo("Netflix") to verify the installation. If the application is found, a boolean value is set to true and Netflix is launched directly. If not found, the boolean remains false and a dialog box is displayed. The method is executed within a function using a try–catch block, as getAppInfo throws a WebAPI exception when the Netflix application is not available, which is handled in the catch block.
